From: Agent Browser contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Android product profile gate for the noise-seed config

rev2: the payload switch is agent-browser-noise-seeds (distinct from the
timezone config switch, whose historical name collides with the first
revision's switch choice). The enabled gate requires BOTH the product
profile switch AND the noise-seeds payload, so desktop behavior is
unchanged and the Android gate is exact.

Runtime acceptance (per-profile canvas/audio divergence on a real device)
remains a separate requirement.

--- a/third_party/blink/public/common/roxy_fingerprint_config.h
+++ b/third_party/blink/public/common/roxy_fingerprint_config.h
@@ -559,10 +559,20 @@
       }
     }
 
+    // The Android product profile provisions the payload through its own
+    // reviewed frozen argv (agent-browser-noise-seeds); its payloads
+    // carry only per-profile canvas/audio differentiation seeds, so the
+    // desktop platform/UA gates do not apply there. The gate requires
+    // BOTH the product profile switch AND the noise-seeds payload, so
+    // desktop behavior is unchanged and the Android gate is exact.
+    const bool agent_browser_product_noise_profile =
+        command_line->HasSwitch("agent-browser-product-profile") &&
+        command_line->HasSwitch("agent-browser-noise-seeds");
     enabled_ = seed_ > 0 &&
-               (platform_ == "Win32" || platform_ == "MacIntel") &&
-               !user_agent_.empty() && !languages_.empty() &&
-               hardware_concurrency_ > 0 && device_memory_ > 0;
+               (agent_browser_product_noise_profile ||
+                ((platform_ == "Win32" || platform_ == "MacIntel") &&
+                 !user_agent_.empty() && !languages_.empty() &&
+                 hardware_concurrency_ > 0 && device_memory_ > 0));
   }
 
   static std::string ReadString(const base::DictValue& dict,
